  partName: Ignition Coil (2)
  description: The Ignition Coil (2) is a second ignition coil located at the top-center-center
    of the engine, which works in conjunction with the first ignition coil to provide
    a reliable spark to the spark plugs. Made from Material.001, this tiny, complex-shaped
    part is vital for maintaining optimal engine performance, and its central location
    allows for efficient energy transfer. Interestingly, the ignition coil's complex
    shape helps to optimize its magnetic field and increase spark energy, even at
    high engine speeds.
